{# Pages that are online and still say what the installer wrote in them.

   Included by the page list and by the dashboard, from the same service: the
   dashboard is where somebody notices, the list is where they act, and two
   copies of the wording would drift.

   Not a live region: it is part of the page from the moment it loads, reachable
   by its heading, and announcing it out of turn would talk over whatever the
   reader came to do. The heading level is given by the including screen, so the
   outline of each stays in order.

   Links carry `alert-link`: the brand colour of the theme reads at 2.9:1 on this
   background, and a link nobody can read is a warning nobody acts on. #}
{% set level = sample_text_heading_level|default(2) %}
{% if sample_text_pages.total > 0 %}
    <div class="alert alert-warning" data-testid="cms-sample-text-warning">
        <h{{ level }} class="h6 alert-heading">
            <i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle-fill me-1" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            {{ 'Some pages are online with our example text still on them'|trans({}, 'theliacms') }}
        </h{{ level }}>
        <p class="mb-2">
            {{ 'Visitors read these pages, and so do search engines. Open each one and write it, or take it offline until it is written.'|trans({}, 'theliacms') }}
        </p>
        <ul class="mb-0">
            {% for page in sample_text_pages.pages %}
                <li>
                    <a class="alert-link" href="{{ path('admin.cms.pages.builder', { id: page.id, edit_language_id: page.language_id }) }}">{{- page.title -}}</a>
                    <span>({{ page.language }})</span>
                </li>
            {% endfor %}
        </ul>
        {% if sample_text_pages.total > sample_text_pages.pages|length %}
            <p class="mb-0 mt-2">
                {{ 'And %count% more.'|trans({'%count%': sample_text_pages.total - sample_text_pages.pages|length}, 'theliacms') }}
            </p>
        {% endif %}
    </div>
{% endif %}
